    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__860" type="place">OAKLAND</rs> 13
                            <!-- Punkt in Zeilenmitte --><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__848"
                            type="place">CALIFORNIA</rs>
                        <lb/><date when="1946-07-07">July 7, 1946</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr.
                    Tillich</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>It is a number of years since we met in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__831"
                        type="place">Carmel</rs>. <hi rend="g">That</hi> I met you encourages me to
                    send you today a translation of mine which I have just completed.<note type="ea"
                        >Liegt nicht vor.</note> It is <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1407"
                        type="person">Novalis</rs>&apos; <hi rend="u"><rs ref="#tillich__E8B2N8XT"
                            type="work">Die Christenheit oder Europa</rs></hi>.</p>
                <p>This essay seems to me one of the most beautiful pieces of German prose in regard
                    to form as well as to content. It contains a good deal of timely and prophetic
                    wisdom.</p>
                <p>Don&apos;t<!-- im Text: <q>D'ont</q> --> you think that <hi rend="u">The Review of
                        Religion</hi> would be an appropriate <sic>magazin</sic> for publication?
                    And furthermore, in case you should like my translation would you be willing to
                    hand it on with a <sic>recommandation</sic>? Do you feel that such a publication
                    would ask for a general short introduction and if you think so would you have
                    any suggestion who would be willing and equipped to write it?</p>
                <p>You can imagine that I am most interested in your reaction since there are not
                    many people in this country who can judge <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1407"
                        type="person">Novalis</rs> text from a literary as well as from a religious
                    point of view.</p>
                <p>Will you permit me to add one personal note, because this translation may come
                    somewhat unexpectedly to you. In the fall or winter issue of the <hi rend="u"
                        >Journal of the History of Ideas</hi> you will find an essay of mine <rs
                        ref="#tillich__DHC64D5W" type="work"><q>The Landscape Garden as a Symbol in
                        Rousseau, Goethe and Flaubert</q></rs>, this I am mentioning in order to give
                    you an idea what I have done during these last years. <!--[...]--></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
